    "prose": "Raid an Enemy Beacon\nWritten from a built-in template.\nWalk to your core, place an Attack beacon beside it, and send its raiders against the nearest enemy beacon you know of.\n\nRoute\n  1. to_core: walk to beacon \"b_00\".\n  2. place_raid: place a beacon at a site covering the nearest scrap seam (nearest by travel, read when the step starts), tagged \"raid\", on an Attack mandate: attacking the nearest known enemy beacon (chosen when the force launches), retargeting the nearest known enemy beacon, gathering at voxel 192, 192, 0, launching once 2 raiders stand there, breaking off once fewer than 51% of the force remain, then regrouping at the staging point and in 1 wave, at normal Quartermaster priority (19 s on site).\n    Give up after 1:00.\n    On failure, move on to the next step.\n  3. hold: hold for 30 s.\n\nRules\n  1. \"flee\", when the commander is at or below 40% HP and the commander took damage in the last 3 s:\n    1. flee_to_safety: walk to the safest own beacon.\n    2. flee_wait: hold for 8 s.\n    Then carry on with the route.\n    Fires at most 3 times, and no sooner than every 30 s.\n\nIf the commander dies\n  On respawn, carry on from the step the route was on.\n\nFallback\n  Hold at the safest own beacon.\n\nBudget\n  6 of 128 size units.\n  19 s standing at a beacon along the route.\n",
